    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109-a1-a2">

                <pb facs="0218" n="148" xml:id="pg148"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Earl Russell</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-07-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 7, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> In answer to your lordship’s note of
                    the 4th instant, requesting me to inform you of the exact date at which a
                    demand, similar to that made by me in the case of the Emily St. Pierre, was made
                    by the British government upon that of the United States, I have the honor to
                    transmit a copy of the note of Mr. Liston to Mr. Pickering, dated at
                    Philadelphia, February 2, 1800, as I find it printed in the 3d volume of the
                    State Papers of the United States relating to foreign affairs.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, my lord, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl Russell.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
